  "script": {
    "segments": [
      {
        "narration": "A massive iron pillar built 1,600 years ago refuses to rust. Standing in outdoor heat and monsoon moisture, raw iron should decay within decades.",
        "visual_query": "qutb complex delhi iron pillar",
        "visual_fallback": "ancient iron tower"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Ancient blacksmiths had no modern rustproofing or stainless steel. Yet while other ancient metal crumbled away, this six-ton pillar remained untouched.",
        "visual_query": "ancient indian blacksmith forging iron",
        "visual_fallback": "blacksmith fire sparks"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Did ancient metallurgists unlock secret technology modern science forgot? For centuries, people believed divine magic or extraterrestrial metal protected it.",
        "visual_query": "gupta empire ancient indian temple",
        "visual_fallback": "ancient stone ruin"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Microscopic analysis finally solved the mystery. High phosphorus content left over from ancient smelting methods triggered a rare protective chemical shield.",
        "visual_query": "laboratory scientist analyzing metal surface",
        "visual_fallback": "microscope research lab"
      },
      {
        "narration": "It formed an airtight layer of iron hydrogen phosphate, blocking corrosion forever. Did those ancient smiths deliberately engineer this armor, or was it a total accident?",
        "visual_query": "ancient iron pillar quwwat ul islam",
        "visual_fallback": "historic landmark sun"
      }
